      "check_name": "PermitAttributes",
      "message": "Potentially dangerous key allowed for mass assignment",
      "file": "app/controllers/api/waitlist_signups_controller.rb",
      "line": 27,
      "note": "False positive. Brakeman flags :role on the name alone, matching its heuristic for an authorization role. WaitlistSignup#role carries no authorization meaning -- it is a self-declared signup preference ('owner', 'sitter', 'both') used only to segment the waitlist and to pick which copy the welcome email shows. It grants nothing. It is also constrained by `validates :role, inclusion: { in: ROLES }` in app/models/waitlist_signup.rb, so an attacker cannot write an arbitrary value. Authorization in this app is session-based (app/controllers/concerns/authentication.rb) or HTTP Basic for admin (app/controllers/api/admin_controller.rb), and neither consults this column."
    }
